# POSITION AXIS: the mutating call is inside a `meta for`-GENERATED MATCH ARM.
#
# `meta` bodies expand during IR lowering, AFTER the semantic pass has run, so
# the expanded call site has no typed classification of its own — the arm's
# pattern binding has no resolved type until the expansion happens. The CoW
# prescan therefore gets no per-call answer here, and what it does with that
# is the whole question.
#
# The answer is the self-host's, which states the direction explicitly:
# absent ⇒ MUTATING, "over-clones, never UAFs; the absent ⇒ read-only
# direction is the unsound one and is NOT used" (`lower.gg`,
# `method_mutates_receiver` step 3).
#
# ⚠ THIS FIXTURE IS THE REASON THAT DIRECTION IS NOT NEGOTIABLE. Measured on
# the pre-fix compiler, this shape was rescued ONLY by the mutator's NAME
# being on the retired `MUTATING_METHODS` hand list: rename `grow` to `resize`
# and the same program returned 0. An unclassified-⇒-read-only fallback made
# BOTH names rc 139 — a REGRESSION against stock, caught by the miss counter
# (`GG_REPORT_RECV_MUT=1`, which prints one `[recv-mut-miss] <name>` per
# unclassified query) rather than by any test.
#
# RED-verified twice: rc 139 pre-fix (C AND LLVM) under the unlisted name, and
# rc 139 again under an unclassified-⇒-read-only fallback under BOTH names.
#
# ⚠ NO ggdef ADJUDICATION — OUT OF SUBSET (Core #9 note). The oracle rejects
# this shape: ``meta for` match arms are phase 2`
# (`spec/ggdef/src/elaborate/mod.rs`). Verify:
#   cargo run -q -p ggdef --release -- run tests/fixtures/cow_user_mutator_meta_generated_arm.gg
# So the evidence here is C + LLVM + the self-host lowerer lane agreeing, which
# Core #8 rates necessary-not-sufficient. The subset gap is filed as
# `todo/t0762`; `lib/xtd/dataframe.gg` writes real stdlib code in this shape,
# so the unadjudicated surface is not exotic.
String mk(String a, String b):
    return a + b

struct Holder:
    Vector[String] items

equip Holder:
    void grow(&self):
        int i = 0
        while i < 64:
            self.items.push(mk("xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx", "yyyyyyyyyyyyyyyy"))
            i = i + 1

enum Wrap:
    One(Holder)

equip Wrap:
    String probe(&self):
        match self:
            meta for vname, T in variant_payloads(Wrap):
                case vname(h):
                    String s = h.items.get(0).unwrap()
                    h.grow()
                    return s

void main():
    Wrap w = Wrap.One(Holder([mk("hello", "world")]))
    print(w.probe())
